## A debate

You (this chat) and a routed model take turns on one transcript file. Default two rounds of
critique: critique, your response, refutation, your response, then your picks. Stop early when the
critic's first line is `NO NEW OBJECTION`. The user may ask for three rounds; never more than four
(later rounds mostly repeat, and each one costs a call).

1. Write the draft (or the user's material) to `~/Bonsai/debate-<topic>.md` under a heading `# Draft`.
2. Round 1: `bonsai pass <model> -f ~/Bonsai/debate-<topic>.md -o ~/Bonsai/debate-<topic>.r1.md`; append
   its answer to the transcript under `# Critique 1`.
3. Write your response under `# Response 1`: answer each finding, conceding or rebutting it with a reason.
4. Round 2 and on: `bonsai pass <model> --round 2 -f ~/Bonsai/debate-<topic>.md -o ~/Bonsai/debate-<topic>.r2.md`;
